title: The Adventure template
intro: Where's Pip? A short point-and-click adventure across three rooms, with someone to talk to, things to find, use and put together, and an ending, all with no code.
project: Adventure | Wheres Pip

chapter: The kitchen | Hotspots, items and a door to the garden
scene: Kitchen
say: Pip the cat has been out all night. The Adventure template is a short adventure to find him, made of hotspots, items and rooms.
select: Kettle
explain: component:UseWith | Use With | The kettle fills a mug with tea: a Use With for the cup, which gives tea back.
select: Back Door
explain: field:Hotspot.GoesTo | Goes To | The back door is a hotspot that goes to the garden. Using it fades out, and the hero arrives at the garden's own back door, its Arrive At.
deselect
play
wait: 1.0
expectvalue: Player.Dialogue.IsTalking = true
explain: game | The first words | The first time, the hero says why we're here. A click moves it on.
gameclick: 0, -0.5
wait: 0.4
gameclick: 0, -0.5
wait: 0.4
gameclick: 0, -0.5
wait: 0.4
gameclick: 0, -0.5
wait: 0.4
gameclick: 0, -0.5
wait: 0.4
gameclick: 0, -0.5
wait: 0.6
expectvalue: Player.Dialogue.IsTalking = false
gameclick: Cup
wait: 3.0
expectvalue: Player.Walker.Said = I'll take my mug.
gamebutton: item:Cup
wait: 0.3
expectvalue: Player.InventoryBar.Holding = Cup
gameclick: Kettle
wait: 3.0
expectvalue: Player.Walker.Said = One nice hot cup of tea, coming up.
explain: game | Tea | Picked from the bar and used on the kettle, the mug comes back full of tea.
gameclick: Back Door
wait: 4.0
expectvalue: Mabel.Hotspot.UseTalks = true
explain: game | The garden | Out in the garden: Pip up the apple tree, Mabel over the fence, and Grandad's shed, locked.
stop

chapter: Mabel and the ending | A talk with choices, and a trigger that ends it
scene: Garden
select: Mabel
explain: field:Dialogue.Lines | Choices | Mabel's lines offer choices and remember what was said with flags. Her Use With for the tea starts her talk again, and gives back the shed key.
select: The End
explain: component:Trigger | Load Scene | When Pip's talk is over, its message sets off this trigger, and its Load Scene goes to the ending.
deselect
play
wait: 1.0
gamebutton: item:Tea
wait: 0.3
gameclick: Mabel
wait: 3.0
expectvalue: Mabel.UseWith.TimesUsed = 1
gameclick: 0, -0.5
wait: 0.4
gameclick: 0, -0.5
wait: 0.4
gameclick: 0, -0.5
wait: 0.4
gameclick: 0, -0.5
wait: 0.6
expectvalue: Mabel.Dialogue.IsTalking = false
explain: game | The shed key | The key's in the bar now. The shed, the fishing rod and a sardine on its line bring Pip down, and the game remembers it all between runs.
stop
